WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.330
CHUCK: <i>On April 21st. 1967.</i>

2
00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:07.787
<i>the hundred-millionth GM vehicle</i>

3
00:00:07.908 --> 00:00:09.877
<i>rolled off the line at
the plant in Janesville.</i>

4
00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.410
<i>Three days later. another
car rolled off that same line.</i>

5
00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.844
<i>This 1967 Chevrolet Impala</i>

6
00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.280
<i>would turn out to be
the most important object</i>

7
00:00:17.451 --> 00:00:19.477
<i>- in pretty much the whole universe.</i>
- Whoo!

8
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:20.979
DEAN: <i>Listen to her purr.</i>

9
00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.284
- This is the car you want.
- Oh. yeah?

10
00:00:27.461 --> 00:00:28.838
You... You know
something about cars?

11
00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.422
My dad taught me
everything about cars.

12
00:00:30.664 --> 00:00:32.462
- (TIRES SCREECHING)
- (HORN HONKING)

13
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.160
I know it's been a long time.

14
00:00:34.268 --> 00:00:38.035
<i>Dean and I... We've... We've been through
a lot of bad. But this is different.</i>

15
00:00:38.205 --> 00:00:40.140
<i>This is my fault and I
don't know how to fix it.</i>

16
00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:42.173
We need your help. God.

17
00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.576
We need to know there's hope.

18
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

19
00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:57.685
(TRAIN ENGINE CHUGGING)

20
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:24.511
(TRAIN HORN BLOWING)

21
00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:46.597
SAM: <i>Hey.</i> DEAN: Hey.

22
00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.409
SAM: <i>Dude. what's
up with the shorts?</i>

23
00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.611
- DEAN: It's a free bunker.
- (SAM SCOFFS)

24
00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.211
DEAN: Did you find
anything? SAM: Uh...

25
00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.511
SAM: Not on The Darkness.

26
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.649
No. (GRUNTS)

27
00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.381
DEAN: What about Metatron?

28
00:02:00.554 --> 00:02:03.353
SAM: Still in the
wind. No leads.

29
00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.582
DEAN: Great.

30
00:02:04.758 --> 00:02:06.693
So. we have an ancient
evil out there somewhere.

31
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.193
just getting
stronger by the day.

32
00:02:09.363 --> 00:02:11.764
Cass is getting
better. so there's that.

33
00:02:11.932 --> 00:02:13.652
- Still wants to fix your. uh...
- I'm fine.

34
00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:14.861
Fine. 100%.

35
00:02:15.035 --> 00:02:17.698
All right. well. he's not. He
still needs more time to heal.

36
00:02:18.205 --> 00:02:21.835
Well... (GRUNTS) Guess we
got nothing to do but get better.

37
00:02:22.009 --> 00:02:25.571
I don't know about you. but
I've got some serious cabin fever.

38
00:02:25.746 --> 00:02:27.186
I've washed every
car in here twice.

39
00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.125
Well. I may have
found us a case.

40
00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.516
- I mean. it's thin...
- Hey. thin works.

41
00:02:31.685 --> 00:02:32.685
Tell me on the way.

42
00:02:41.695 --> 00:02:42.719
Figures.

43
00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.876
All right. let's hear
it. What do you got?

44
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:49.770
Okay. uh. Quaker Valley.
Oregon. town outside of Eugene.

45
00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:53.003
Dwayne Markham. the local sheriff.
was found in the woods a couple days ago.

46
00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.585
His body was mauled. so they
chalked it up to an animal attack.

47
00:02:55.609 --> 00:02:56.889
- but I'm thinking...
- Werewolf.

48
00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.979
- Yeah. maybe.
- Yeah. you're right. That is thin.

49
00:02:59.146 --> 00:03:00.614
Yeah. Probably nothing. right?

50
00:03:00.781 --> 00:03:01.874
Probably not.

51
00:03:02.049 --> 00:03:03.049
Oregon. here we come.

52
00:03:17.264 --> 00:03:18.264
What is that?

53
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.500
It's a smoothie.

54
00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.239
Where's the beer?

55
00:03:30.077 --> 00:03:31.077
Under the smoothies.

56
00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.407
Where's the rest of the beer?

57
00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.307
(CELL PHONE RINGS)

58
00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.294
- Ooh. it's Cass. We gotta. we gotta...
- Man.

59
00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:39.318
I gotta get this.

60
00:03:39.653 --> 00:03:41.178
Hey. Cass. Everything all right?

61
00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.561
CASTIEL: <i>Yeah. I'm fine.
I was just reading up about</i>

62
00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.750
<i>the other cases in the
area that you're headed to.</i>

63
00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.224
<i>I haven't found anything
yet that matches.</i>

64
00:03:48.395 --> 00:03:50.206
Cass. you've got one
job to do and that's to heal.

65
00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.926
- You understand?
- CASTIEL: <i>I can help.</i>

66
00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:53.242
Yeah. of course you can. Cass.

67
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:57.033
but. right now is the time for
you to focus on getting better.

68
00:03:57.204 --> 00:04:01.141
This is just a milk run.
We got it. So. try and relax.

69
00:04:01.308 --> 00:04:02.867
- CASTIEL: <i>All right.</i>
- Read a book.

70
00:04:03.043 --> 00:04:04.477
Watch some Netflix.

71
00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.170
<i>- What's a "Netflix"?</i>
- (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

72
00:04:08.215 --> 00:04:11.151
Go to my room. turn on
the TV. You'll figure it out.

73
00:04:11.485 --> 00:04:12.714
<i>All right.</i>

74
00:04:12.886 --> 00:04:14.718
<i>Just call if you need anything.</i>

75
00:04:14.888 --> 00:04:16.356
Got it. Cass. Thanks.

76
00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.821
You think he's gonna be okay?

77
00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.922
He just needs some
time. you know? We all do.

78
00:04:35.876 --> 00:04:36.876
Are you serious?

79
00:04:38.512 --> 00:04:43.041
Dean. it's late. I'm exhausted
and. and... And starving.

80
00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.912
And this place...

81
00:04:45.085 --> 00:04:47.987
I mean. even Swayze wouldn't
come to this Roadhouse.

82
00:04:48.155 --> 00:04:50.715
Okay. first of all. never
use Swayze's name in vain.

83
00:04:50.891 --> 00:04:51.915
- Okay? Ever.
- (SCOFFS)

84
00:04:52.092 --> 00:04:53.812
DEAN: <i>Second. you
don't remember this place?</i>

85
00:04:55.095 --> 00:04:56.290
You don't remember Heather?

86
00:04:57.097 --> 00:04:59.275
The hunter that we worked a
Wendigo case a couple years ago?

87
00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.029
- Oh. yeah.
- Yeah. exactly.

88
00:05:01.201 --> 00:05:02.294
What. she's here tonight?

89
00:05:02.469 --> 00:05:06.406
I texted her. She's working
a rugaru case in Texas.

90
00:05:06.573 --> 00:05:08.518
Actually. she never texted
me back. That's not the point.

91
00:05:08.542 --> 00:05:11.444
The point is. is that we
have a ton of driving left to do

92
00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:14.342
just to go to a town where
there's probably not a case.

93
00:05:15.649 --> 00:05:18.141
But in there. good times.

94
00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:22.888
And time heals all wounds.
Sam. especially good times.

95
00:05:23.857 --> 00:05:24.881
What do you say?

96
00:05:27.294 --> 00:05:28.557
I say. knock yourself out.

97
00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.630
I'm gonna find a diner. dig
into the lore like Cass did.

98
00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:34.666
see if anything's ever
happened where we're headed.

99
00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.781
Oh. man. you really gotta
learn how to have fun.

100
00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.531
Seriously. it's pathetic.

101
00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:43.069
(BLUES SONG PLAYING)

102
00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:10.701
(SAM GROANS)

103
00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:14.439
Mistakes were made. Mmm-hmm.

104
00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:17.837
Who are you?

105
00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:19.973
- Oh.
- SAM: Uh. good morning.

106
00:06:20.614 --> 00:06:22.981
SAM: (CLEARS THROAT)
<i>That's. uh. my brother Dean.</i>

107
00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:25.550
Sorry. Sam. I didn't. I didn't
realize you had company.

108
00:06:25.719 --> 00:06:27.688
SAM: <i>Yeah. Yeah. could
you give us a minute?</i>

109
00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:28.854
Hi.

110
00:06:29.656 --> 00:06:32.125
Well. I'll just. uh... Just
won't be here anymore.

111
00:06:32.292 --> 00:06:34.284
So. you kids take your time.

112
00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:45.665
Have you seen my hairpin?

113
00:06:50.043 --> 00:06:52.603
- Dean. I can explain what was going on...
- No. no. no. No.

114
00:06:53.847 --> 00:06:55.645
<i>(NIGHT MOVES</i> PLAYING)

115
00:06:58.919 --> 00:07:01.479
- Don't <i>Night Moves</i> me.
- Shh.

116
00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:03.456
Just let it wash over you.

117
00:07:03.924 --> 00:07:05.449
- Look...
- Just take it in.

118
00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.260
(SAM CHUCKLES)

119
00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.092
(MOUTHING LYRICS)

120
00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:22.465
This is ridiculous.

121
00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.944
One of the greatest rock
writers of all time. Samuel.

122
00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:30.182
It's Sam.

123
00:07:38.725 --> 00:07:41.889
(SINGING)

124
00:07:42.629 --> 00:07:44.928
You started this.
You started this.

125
00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:49.192
Here we go. Come on now.

126
00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:52.264
(BOTH SINGING)

127
00:07:56.176 --> 00:07:57.508
(BOTH LAUGHING)

128
00:07:59.079 --> 00:08:00.308
Next time. I choose.

129
00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.073
- Hey.
- Hands off the wheel.

130
00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.222
You're not even
looking at the road.

131
00:08:12.726 --> 00:08:13.726
"Digging into the lore."

132
00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.705
Is that what the kids
are calling it these days?

133
00:08:15.729 --> 00:08:16.729
(SAM CHUCKLES)

134
00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:18.390
Man. I needed that.

135
00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:19.891
(DEAN CHUCKLES)

136
00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.311
And hey. look at that. you're
finally not a virgin anymore.

137
00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:23.746
But you know what?
I think it was time.

138
00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.648
- I respect the fact that you. uh...
- (CHUCKLES)

139
00:08:25.672 --> 00:08:28.107
You know. you wanted to
stay true and pure and waited.

140
00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:30.004
Yeah. you know
what? You're an idiot.

141
00:08:30.777 --> 00:08:32.040
Even put a blanket down.

142
00:08:32.212 --> 00:08:35.182
Buddy. classy and
thoughtful as always.

143
00:08:36.583 --> 00:08:37.846
I tried to give her my number.

144
00:08:39.486 --> 00:08:40.486
You know what she said?

145
00:08:41.221 --> 00:08:42.701
"We got tonight. Who
needs tomorrow?"

146
00:08:45.692 --> 00:08:47.661
Is everything a Bob
Seger song to you?

147
00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:49.461
Yes.

148
00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:53.197
(INHALES DEEPLY)

149
00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.737
Well... (SIGHS) It was
nice knowing you. Piper.

150
00:08:58.471 --> 00:08:59.471
Piper?

151
00:09:00.473 --> 00:09:02.806
(LAUGHS) That's awesome.

152
00:09:03.109 --> 00:09:06.307
- (BOTH CHUCKLE)
- Heather. One-night wonders. man.

153
00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:10.180
Shoot. we're lucky
we still get that at all.

154
00:09:12.886 --> 00:09:17.051
Really? You don't ever
want something more?

155
00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:20.491
I'm sorry. have you met us?

156
00:09:21.061 --> 00:09:24.463
We're batting a whopping zero
in domestic life. man. Goose eggs.

157
00:09:25.432 --> 00:09:30.063
You don't ever think about
something? Not marriage or whatever.

158
00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:34.867
But. something. you know. with a hunter?
Somebody who understands the life?

159
00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:37.340
Have you not heard a single
word Bob's been singing about?

160
00:09:39.612 --> 00:09:41.547
You're tired. I can
tell. You're exhausted.

161
00:09:42.816 --> 00:09:44.794
Well. I'm still wired. so I'm
gonna pull over. get some gas.

162
00:09:44.818 --> 00:09:48.050
You hop in the back. get some
Z's. 'cause. buddy. you earned 'em.

163
00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:50.813
Proud of you! Piper.

164
00:09:51.391 --> 00:09:53.383
<i>Mmm. Man. she smelled good. too.</i>

165
00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.025
<i>(SOMEDAY SOON</i>
PLAYING ON THE STEREO)

166
00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:11.971
(YAWNS)

167
00:10:13.246 --> 00:10:15.340
What are you listening to?

168
00:10:15.515 --> 00:10:17.882
JOHN: Your mom
used to love this song.

169
00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:20.813
SAM: <i>Dad?</i>

170
00:10:22.188 --> 00:10:26.182
You okay. pal? You
look a little spooked.

171
00:10:44.277 --> 00:10:46.143
It's nice to be back
behind the wheel.

172
00:10:47.046 --> 00:10:49.606
Looks like Dean's taken
good care of this old beast.

173
00:10:51.151 --> 00:10:53.052
Seems like he's taken
good care of you. too.

174
00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:57.790
What is this? Another vision?

175
00:10:58.057 --> 00:10:59.355
Are you having visions. son?

176
00:10:59.859 --> 00:11:00.859
Don't call me that.

177
00:11:02.896 --> 00:11:05.832
- What? A father can't call his...
- No. my father is dead.

178
00:11:06.366 --> 00:11:08.767
When has death ever
stopped a Winchester?

179
00:11:10.737 --> 00:11:12.797
Look. I don't know
what this is. but...

180
00:11:12.972 --> 00:11:16.636
What you said about relationships.
wanting something more...

181
00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.845
I never wanted this for
you boys. this life. Not really.

182
00:11:29.155 --> 00:11:30.453
We turned out okay.

183
00:11:31.324 --> 00:11:33.884
(CHUCKLES) You did. didn't you?

184
00:11:35.295 --> 00:11:38.595
But that was on you
boys. You did that. not me.

185
00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.226
Well. you played your
part. (CHUCKLES)

186
00:11:42.602 --> 00:11:46.369
I did my best. anyway.
for what it was worth.

187
00:11:48.675 --> 00:11:49.904
This isn't real.

188
00:11:56.049 --> 00:11:57.847
I never could fool you. could I?

189
00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:05.355
I prayed when I
was in that church.

190
00:12:06.326 --> 00:12:10.229
And I saw something.

191
00:12:14.634 --> 00:12:20.767
And now. here you are. whoever
you are. whatever you are.

192
00:12:22.642 --> 00:12:23.803
What the hell is this?

193
00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.510
Dream.

194
00:12:26.312 --> 00:12:28.008
Vision. Call it what you want.

195
00:12:28.915 --> 00:12:31.942
<i>The message is still the same.</i>

196
00:12:34.921 --> 00:12:36.617
The Darkness is coming.

197
00:12:42.962 --> 00:12:44.658
Only you boys can stop it.

198
00:12:46.399 --> 00:12:47.628
SAM: Okay. fine.

199
00:12:48.568 --> 00:12:49.568
How?

200
00:12:51.537 --> 00:12:55.304
We need help. not
visions of dead people.

201
00:12:58.177 --> 00:13:01.944
God helps those
who help themselves.

202
00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:06.451
Who are you?

203
00:13:06.986 --> 00:13:08.215
(HORN HONKING)

204
00:13:09.022 --> 00:13:10.081
(INHALES SHARPLY)

205
00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.888
Welcome to the Winchester Motel.

206
00:13:13.926 --> 00:13:18.864
We don't have cable. but
we do have room service.

207
00:13:22.335 --> 00:13:23.667
You were singing in your sleep.

208
00:13:24.971 --> 00:13:28.100
That song Mom loved. Dad
used to always play for us.

209
00:13:28.508 --> 00:13:30.148
I think I've actually
still got the tape.

210
00:13:32.645 --> 00:13:34.409
Hey. Dean. um...

211
00:13:36.916 --> 00:13:40.580
You said when you saw The Darkness.
you weren't sure whether it was. uh...

212
00:13:41.921 --> 00:13:43.685
The real thing
or a vision. right?

213
00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.519
Mmm-hmm.

214
00:13:46.292 --> 00:13:48.784
I think I've been having
visions. too. lately.

215
00:13:49.495 --> 00:13:53.956
I mean. it's just images. I
mean. more of a feeling. really.

216
00:13:55.168 --> 00:13:58.468
But I just had one right now.

217
00:13:58.671 --> 00:14:01.231
and. and Dad was in it.

218
00:14:01.507 --> 00:14:05.410
But it wasn't Dad like. like.
the Dad that. that I grew up with.

219
00:14:05.578 --> 00:14:07.604
It was Dad when he was our age.

220
00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.300
And I guess it wasn't
even really Dad.

221
00:14:09.449 --> 00:14:11.093
It was someone
pretending to be Dad and...

222
00:14:11.117 --> 00:14:12.585
Okay. what makes you say that?

223
00:14:12.752 --> 00:14:15.153
For starters. he told me
everything I wanted to hear.

224
00:14:15.588 --> 00:14:17.352
- Yeah. doesn't sound like Dad.
<i>- No.</i>

225
00:14:17.623 --> 00:14:19.319
Anyways. whoever it was.

226
00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:24.190
they had a message to deliver.

227
00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:26.825
They said The
Darkness is coming.

228
00:14:28.201 --> 00:14:32.002
And only you and I can stop it.

229
00:14:32.705 --> 00:14:35.231
Did they happen to give you
any helpful tips on how to do that?

230
00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:37.806
He said. "God helps those
who help themselves."

231
00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:44.950
I mean. maybe these
visions are coming from God.

232
00:14:45.351 --> 00:14:46.512
Whoa.

233
00:14:46.919 --> 00:14:47.943
Pump the brakes.

234
00:14:48.187 --> 00:14:50.227
I mean. Dean. the first
one happened after I prayed.

235
00:14:51.991 --> 00:14:53.459
You prayed? When was this?

236
00:14:55.495 --> 00:14:56.495
Back in the hospital.

237
00:14:57.597 --> 00:14:58.597
Why?

238
00:15:01.768 --> 00:15:03.031
Because I was infected.

239
00:15:05.405 --> 00:15:07.601
I <i>was</i> infected. I'm not anymore.

240
00:15:07.774 --> 00:15:09.902
And I. I never went full rabid.

241
00:15:11.043 --> 00:15:13.035
You get infected and
you didn't even tell me.

242
00:15:14.013 --> 00:15:15.675
- Dean...
- What did you pray about?

243
00:15:20.887 --> 00:15:22.807
I guess I was just looking
for answers. you know?

244
00:15:25.191 --> 00:15:28.423
Well. I'm sure whatever is kicking
around in your head right now

245
00:15:28.594 --> 00:15:32.690
is a side effect from the infection
that you failed to tell me about.

246
00:15:32.865 --> 00:15:35.027
You know. I don't
think it's that simple.

247
00:15:35.735 --> 00:15:37.601
Come on. man. That quote?

248
00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:40.968
"God helps those who help
themselves"? God didn't say that.

249
00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.369
That's not even in the Bible.

250
00:15:43.009 --> 00:15:45.911
That's an old proverb that
dates way back to Aesop.

251
00:15:48.214 --> 00:15:49.214
I read.

252
00:15:49.916 --> 00:15:51.326
And more importantly.
when was the last time

253
00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.818
God answered any
one of our prayers?

254
00:15:54.787 --> 00:15:59.088
It's not a vision. Sam. All right?
It's just some... Some fever dream.

255
00:16:00.726 --> 00:16:01.785
<i>That's all.</i>

256
00:16:01.994 --> 00:16:05.522
And as far as Dad goes. I
dream about Dad all the time.

257
00:16:07.099 --> 00:16:08.590
- You do?
- Of course I do.

258
00:16:09.469 --> 00:16:11.165
It's usually the same one. too.

259
00:16:11.938 --> 00:16:14.016
We're all in the car. I'm
sitting in the driver's seat.

260
00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.635
Dad's sitting shotgun. But
there aren't any shotguns.

261
00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:20.150
There's no monsters. There's
no hunting. There's none of that.

262
00:16:20.947 --> 00:16:21.947
<i>It's just...</i>

263
00:16:23.282 --> 00:16:24.580
He's teaching me how to drive.

264
00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:29.217
And. uh... And I'm not little like I was
when he actually taught me how to drive.

265
00:16:29.388 --> 00:16:32.222
I'm 16. and he's helping
me get my learner's permit.

266
00:16:32.758 --> 00:16:35.070
Of course. you're in the backseat.
just begging to take a turn.

267
00:16:35.094 --> 00:16:37.461
We pull up to the
house. the family house.

268
00:16:39.065 --> 00:16:41.466
And I park in the driveway.
and he looks over and he says.

269
00:16:42.335 --> 00:16:43.462
"Perfect landing. son."

270
00:16:46.539 --> 00:16:49.539
I have that dream every couple of
months. It's kind of comforting. actually.

271
00:16:52.378 --> 00:16:53.710
I always. uh...

272
00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:55.573
(CHUCKLES)

273
00:16:56.516 --> 00:16:57.609
I always dream about Mom.

274
00:17:00.119 --> 00:17:01.679
Usually the same
kind of thing. though.

275
00:17:02.054 --> 00:17:04.717
- Normal life?
- Yeah. Normal life.

276
00:17:06.859 --> 00:17:10.591
But. Dean. this wasn't
just a dream. I'm telling you.

277
00:17:12.365 --> 00:17:17.133
Why would somebody dress up
like Dad to give you a message?

278
00:17:17.436 --> 00:17:18.436
I mean. <i>Dad.</i>

279
00:17:19.105 --> 00:17:21.683
You don't exactly have a history
of listening to what he had to say.

280
00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:24.176
But you said The Darkness
is sending messages to you.

281
00:17:24.343 --> 00:17:27.370
Maybe whatever is the opposite of The
Darkness is sending messages to me.

282
00:17:27.547 --> 00:17:29.027
And you think that
this thing is God?

283
00:17:30.349 --> 00:17:33.342
Come on. How many. how many opportunities
has God had to crack this piñata.

284
00:17:33.519 --> 00:17:34.830
and I don't see any
candy on the floor. do you?

285
00:17:34.854 --> 00:17:36.618
Okay. then maybe
it's not God. but...

286
00:17:38.124 --> 00:17:39.319
(SIGHS)

287
00:17:39.725 --> 00:17:41.003
I know what you're
trying to do here.

288
00:17:41.027 --> 00:17:44.225
You're trying to find some.
some greater meaning to it all.

289
00:17:44.397 --> 00:17:47.026
Right? Some fate
to what went down.

290
00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:52.236
But I'm telling you. Sam.
The Darkness? It's on us.

291
00:17:53.339 --> 00:17:55.934
<i>And no one's gonna
help us. certainly not God.</i>

292
00:17:56.576 --> 00:18:00.172
so. we'll have to figure this
thing out. like we always do.

293
00:18:01.647 --> 00:18:04.742
But until then. we hunt.

294
00:18:07.086 --> 00:18:10.352
This case. for starters.
Of course. this case is...

295
00:18:10.523 --> 00:18:11.923
Which is probably nothing.

296
00:18:14.493 --> 00:18:15.756
Yeah. probably nothing.

297
00:18:19.732 --> 00:18:20.961
(SIGHS)

298
00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.500
Good night. jerk.

299
00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:25.364
(SMACKS LIPS)

300
00:18:25.771 --> 00:18:26.898
Night. bitch.

301
00:18:27.306 --> 00:18:28.399
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

302
00:18:33.112 --> 00:18:34.112
(SIGHS)

303
00:18:48.961 --> 00:18:51.021
(INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTERING)

304
00:18:53.833 --> 00:18:56.860
Hey. the coroner showed
me the sheriff's body.

305
00:18:57.036 --> 00:18:59.505
And. uh. it was
mauled all right.

306
00:18:59.672 --> 00:19:02.972
And get this. Heart missing.
body completely drained of blood.

307
00:19:03.142 --> 00:19:07.045
So. what? We're looking at
a. a werewolf/vampire hybrid?

308
00:19:07.546 --> 00:19:09.572
- Say it with me. a Were-pire.
- (SIRENS BLARING)

309
00:19:09.849 --> 00:19:10.942
- (CHUCKLES)
- Huh?

310
00:19:11.183 --> 00:19:12.207
No.

311
00:19:12.451 --> 00:19:13.731
- Come on.
- I'm not saying that.

312
00:19:16.822 --> 00:19:18.634
Whatever. I called Cass.
told him to look into the lore.

313
00:19:18.658 --> 00:19:19.658
What do you got?

314
00:19:20.326 --> 00:19:23.558
Right. well. uh. the sheriff's
replacement. Deputy Donnelly...

315
00:19:23.729 --> 00:19:26.289
He's not the brightest bulb.
but I got a copy of his report.

316
00:19:26.832 --> 00:19:28.095
<i>Maybe he missed something.</i>

317
00:19:28.267 --> 00:19:29.267
DONNELLY: <i>Agents.</i>

318
00:19:29.902 --> 00:19:31.097
DEAN: Deputy.

319
00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.761
This must be your partner.

320
00:19:32.938 --> 00:19:33.962
Agent Walsh. right?

321
00:19:34.573 --> 00:19:35.632
<i>Pleasure to meet you.</i>

322
00:19:35.808 --> 00:19:38.039
I just want to thank
you both for stoppin' by.

323
00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.940
We really appreciate
your due diligence.

324
00:19:40.713 --> 00:19:43.513
Oh. Actually. uh. do you know a
motel where we can crash for the night?

325
00:19:44.183 --> 00:19:45.183
You're stayin'?

326
00:19:45.651 --> 00:19:47.620
Yeah. just wanna
kick all the tires.

327
00:19:48.087 --> 00:19:51.489
Well. uh. there's a motel on
Downey that'll give you a good price.

328
00:19:52.058 --> 00:19:53.924
<i>And if you're looking
for a decent meal.</i>

329
00:19:54.093 --> 00:19:57.086
you can't beat Aunt Mel's.
down by the train station.

330
00:19:57.263 --> 00:20:00.927
Parking is a bitch. but it's the
best damn steak in the whole state.

331
00:20:01.701 --> 00:20:02.828
You had me at "steak."

332
00:20:05.638 --> 00:20:07.266
DEAN: (LAUGHS) All right.

333
00:20:07.606 --> 00:20:09.074
Now we're cookin' with gas.

334
00:20:10.776 --> 00:20:11.869
Valet?

335
00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:14.312
You... What?

336
00:20:15.147 --> 00:20:17.707
(CHUCKLES) Dean.
people valet park all the time.

337
00:20:18.484 --> 00:20:19.577
Come on. live a little.

338
00:20:24.323 --> 00:20:25.689
WOMAN: Welcome to Aunt Mel's.

339
00:20:25.958 --> 00:20:27.392
- Home of the...
- Yeah. listen.

340
00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:29.927
Jessie. not a scratch. okay?

341
00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:32.354
(CHUCKLES)

342
00:20:47.413 --> 00:20:48.608
(CHUCKLES)

343
00:20:53.018 --> 00:20:54.816
Spider caught a fly.

344
00:20:54.987 --> 00:20:58.651
I repeat. spider caught a fly.

345
00:20:59.258 --> 00:21:00.385
(CHUCKLES)

346
00:21:01.427 --> 00:21:03.191
- Let's go! Come on!
- JORDAN: Okay!

347
00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:06.463
Hell. yeah. Let's
roll! (GIGGLES)

348
00:21:06.832 --> 00:21:08.994
Let's get this party started.

349
00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:10.327
(BOTH SCREAMING)

350
00:21:16.809 --> 00:21:18.243
Oh. my God!

351
00:21:26.218 --> 00:21:27.218
(LAUGHING)

352
00:21:31.023 --> 00:21:32.218
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

353
00:21:34.994 --> 00:21:37.293
Yes. sir? We're on our way.

354
00:21:38.998 --> 00:21:40.227
My way.

355
00:21:42.368 --> 00:21:43.368
JORDAN: <i>What did you do?</i>

356
00:21:44.436 --> 00:21:45.927
I'm gonna get fired.

357
00:21:46.438 --> 00:21:48.304
JESSIE: Come on! JORDAN: Okay!

358
00:21:49.141 --> 00:21:51.406
- I gotta go. Let's go!
- Where's my purse?

359
00:21:51.577 --> 00:21:53.054
You probably just
left it in your car.

360
00:21:53.078 --> 00:21:55.479
- What?
- I gotta go! I don't wanna get fired!

361
00:21:56.015 --> 00:21:57.039
(GRUNTS)

362
00:22:19.505 --> 00:22:22.270
Strong work.
Jessie. Strong work.

363
00:22:23.509 --> 00:22:24.509
Thanks.

364
00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.404
So. what's next?

365
00:22:30.516 --> 00:22:32.576
I want. uh. to talk to
the sheriff's widow.

366
00:22:36.722 --> 00:22:38.088
Lily Markham.

367
00:22:38.257 --> 00:22:39.601
Maybe she knows something
about why her husband

368
00:22:39.625 --> 00:22:40.969
was out in the woods
in the first place.

369
00:22:40.993 --> 00:22:42.137
All right. well.
I'll drop you off.

370
00:22:42.161 --> 00:22:43.839
I wanna go back to the woods
where they found the body.

371
00:22:43.863 --> 00:22:45.983
Something wasn't right about
those crime scene photos.

372
00:22:47.533 --> 00:22:48.796
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

373
00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:02.504
(GRUNTS)

374
00:23:05.517 --> 00:23:08.146
- Cass. you okay?
- CASTIEL: <i>I'm mostly confused.</i>

375
00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:11.290
<i>I'm not sure how orange correlates
with black in a way that's new.</i>

376
00:23:11.457 --> 00:23:12.891
Step away from the Netflix.

377
00:23:13.325 --> 00:23:15.351
<i>- Sorry.</i>
- It's okay. We've all had a binge.

378
00:23:15.527 --> 00:23:16.927
You find anything in the lore?

379
00:23:17.096 --> 00:23:20.328
<i>Well. there is a creature that
feeds on hearts and blood.</i>

380
00:23:20.499 --> 00:23:21.933
A Were-pire. you might say?

381
00:23:22.101 --> 00:23:23.865
Come on. I know
you wanna say it.

382
00:23:27.306 --> 00:23:29.275
<i>In the lore. it's referred
to as a Whisper.</i>

383
00:23:29.441 --> 00:23:30.534
That's lame.

384
00:23:30.709 --> 00:23:34.009
<i>Silver will kill it. but you may
want to decapitate it just to be sure.</i>

385
00:23:34.179 --> 00:23:36.179
All right. sounds good.
I'm at the crime scene now.

386
00:23:36.348 --> 00:23:39.216
It was staged. The body was dragged.
There were no signs of struggle.

387
00:23:39.551 --> 00:23:41.986
<i>Body was moved there to
look more like an animal attack?</i>

388
00:23:42.154 --> 00:23:44.180
Yeah. maybe. It was
pretty sloppy. though.

389
00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:45.751
You. uh...

390
00:23:45.958 --> 00:23:47.318
What else you got
on these things?

391
00:23:47.526 --> 00:23:49.337
<i>Listen to this. Whispers
have a fascinating history...</i>

392
00:23:49.361 --> 00:23:50.385
Hang on.

393
00:23:51.563 --> 00:23:54.643
CASTIEL: <i>Actually. they were once believed
to be in the bloodline of werewolves.</i>

394
00:23:54.667 --> 00:23:56.465
<i>but in fact. they are
more similar to demons.</i>

395
00:23:56.635 --> 00:23:58.365
DEAN: Deputy? What's going on?

396
00:23:58.537 --> 00:24:02.736
CASTIEL: <i>They. uh... They got their
nickname from how quiet their attacks are.</i>

397
00:24:02.942 --> 00:24:04.719
<i>- Because of their stealthiness...</i>
- (TRAIN HORN BLOWING)

398
00:24:04.743 --> 00:24:07.178
<i>they've. uh. lived on
the fringes for centuries.</i>

399
00:24:07.446 --> 00:24:08.573
<i>Although. there were several</i>

400
00:24:08.747 --> 00:24:11.046
<i>that were hunted and killed
during the Salem witch...</i>

401
00:24:11.317 --> 00:24:13.252
<i>Wait a minute. Okay.
according to this.</i>

402
00:24:13.419 --> 00:24:15.888
<i>Whispers only feed
during a solar eclipse.</i>

403
00:24:16.455 --> 00:24:18.720
<i>Uh. so. Dean.
I... I don't believe</i>

404
00:24:18.924 --> 00:24:20.669
<i>- what you're hunting is a Whisper.</i>
- (DONNELLY GRUNTING)

405
00:24:20.693 --> 00:24:22.974
<i>- Must be another creature of some kind.</i>
- (DEAN GRUNTING)

406
00:24:23.028 --> 00:24:25.224
<i>Okay. Fine. I'll say it.</i>

407
00:24:25.397 --> 00:24:26.397
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

408
00:24:26.699 --> 00:24:28.463
<i>Maybe it is your
so-called Were-pire.</i>

409
00:24:28.701 --> 00:24:32.103
<i>But to be honest. I have never
heard of a creature with that name.</i>

410
00:24:32.371 --> 00:24:34.101
<i>- Dean. what is that?</i>
- (GRUNTS)

411
00:24:35.107 --> 00:24:36.107
<i>Dean?</i>

412
00:24:37.142 --> 00:24:38.735
(BOTH GRUNTING)

413
00:24:40.546 --> 00:24:41.741
(GUN FIRES)

414
00:24:42.047 --> 00:24:45.074
<i>Dean. Dean. are you
all right? I hear gunshots.</i>

415
00:24:45.551 --> 00:24:47.383
<i>- Dean!</i>
- (DEAN GROANING)

416
00:24:49.488 --> 00:24:50.488
<i>Dean?</i>

417
00:24:53.025 --> 00:24:54.152
<i>Dean!</i>

418
00:24:55.761 --> 00:24:57.525
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

419
00:24:58.797 --> 00:25:01.028
Ah. turns out I did
shoot the deputy.

420
00:25:02.201 --> 00:25:05.081
- CASTIEL: <i>Wait. Dean. is. is everything...</i>
- The deputy was a Were-pire.

421
00:25:05.371 --> 00:25:06.371
It's all right.

422
00:25:07.539 --> 00:25:08.734
Silver bullets worked.

423
00:25:09.041 --> 00:25:10.304
<i>No. Dean. listen.</i>

424
00:25:10.609 --> 00:25:12.988
- (DONNELLY GROWLING)
<i>- According to the lore. the timing is off.</i>

425
00:25:13.012 --> 00:25:15.709
<i>The next solar eclipse in
North America is years away.</i>

426
00:25:15.881 --> 00:25:17.042
<i>- It can't be a...</i>
- Hang on.

427
00:25:17.983 --> 00:25:19.178
<i>Dean. wait.</i>

428
00:25:20.819 --> 00:25:22.788
<i>- This thing couldn't be...</i>
- (GRUNTING)

429
00:25:23.188 --> 00:25:24.451
(DONNELLY GROWLING)

430
00:25:24.757 --> 00:25:25.757
<i>Dean?</i>

431
00:25:28.027 --> 00:25:29.154
(DONNELLY GRUNTS)

432
00:25:32.464 --> 00:25:33.932
(GRUNTS)

433
00:25:34.767 --> 00:25:35.767
Scratch that.

434
00:25:36.201 --> 00:25:37.533
You gotta cut off their...

435
00:25:37.936 --> 00:25:39.131
(GROWLING)

436
00:25:40.706 --> 00:25:41.935
(DONNELLY CHOKING)

437
00:25:44.176 --> 00:25:45.974
CASTIEL: <i>Dean.
it's not a Whisper.</i>

438
00:25:48.680 --> 00:25:49.943
Yeah. I'm starting to get that.

439
00:25:50.983 --> 00:25:52.144
Give me a sec.

440
00:25:54.386 --> 00:25:55.513
(GRUNTS)

441
00:26:02.094 --> 00:26:03.094
All right.

442
00:26:03.562 --> 00:26:05.121
(DONNELLY GROWLING)

443
00:26:06.865 --> 00:26:08.128
All right. that...

444
00:26:10.702 --> 00:26:11.761
(GRUNTS)

445
00:26:28.987 --> 00:26:30.785
(DONNELLY CONTINUES GROWLING)

446
00:26:34.927 --> 00:26:36.225
(GROWLING STOPS)

447
00:26:38.831 --> 00:26:40.129
(DEAN GRUNTS)

448
00:26:45.904 --> 00:26:47.463
(MUFFLED GRUNTING)

449
00:26:50.042 --> 00:26:51.203
(DEAN GRUNTS)

450
00:26:52.344 --> 00:26:53.344
Okay.

451
00:26:54.413 --> 00:26:55.904
(DONNELLY GROWLING)

452
00:27:01.053 --> 00:27:02.316
Smile. asshat.

453
00:27:02.621 --> 00:27:04.749
- (DONNELLY GROWLING)
- (CAMERA CLICKING)

454
00:27:07.559 --> 00:27:08.720
(SIGHS)

455
00:27:09.061 --> 00:27:11.860
- All right. Cass. you there?
- CASTIEL: <i>Of course. What's going on?</i>

456
00:27:12.998 --> 00:27:14.933
Well. whatever it is.
silver slows it down.

457
00:27:15.968 --> 00:27:19.837
I. uh... I'm sending you a
picture right now of its fangs.

458
00:27:20.005 --> 00:27:21.325
I've never seen
anything like it.

459
00:27:21.406 --> 00:27:23.206
See if there's a match
in the lore. would you?

460
00:27:23.575 --> 00:27:24.736
CASTIEL: <i>I'm on it.</i>

461
00:27:25.043 --> 00:27:26.043
(SIGHS)

462
00:27:30.916 --> 00:27:32.282
(LINE DIALING)

463
00:27:33.418 --> 00:27:34.750
SAM: <i>Dean. I got jumped.</i>

464
00:27:34.920 --> 00:27:37.754
- You okay?
<i>- I think. for now.</i>

465
00:27:37.923 --> 00:27:39.534
<i>Pretty sure we're
dealing with a pack here.</i>

466
00:27:39.558 --> 00:27:42.198
<i>Uh. two of these things were
attacking Mrs. Markham when I arrived.</i>

467
00:27:42.327 --> 00:27:44.660
<i>I. I filled them with silver.
but it only slowed them down.</i>

468
00:27:44.897 --> 00:27:47.093
Yeah. well. Deputy Dumbass
is one of them as well.

469
00:27:47.266 --> 00:27:50.134
He's. uh... He's in two
pieces and still alive.

470
00:27:50.602 --> 00:27:51.695
Where you at now?

471
00:27:51.970 --> 00:27:54.439
<i>Mrs. Markham was knocked
out. I carried her to a house nearby.</i>

472
00:27:54.606 --> 00:27:57.646
<i>- Here. I'll text you the address now.</i>
- All right. sit tight. I'm on my way.

473
00:28:00.279 --> 00:28:01.372
(GRUNTS)

474
00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:03.776
Buddy's gettin' jumped.

475
00:28:03.982 --> 00:28:05.006
(SIGHS)

476
00:28:24.403 --> 00:28:25.947
SAM: <i>Door was open
when I got to the house.</i>

477
00:28:25.971 --> 00:28:29.100
By the time I searched through it.
they'd already beaten her unconscious.

478
00:28:29.274 --> 00:28:30.274
Maybe she knew something

479
00:28:30.542 --> 00:28:32.053
or something about what
happened to her husband.

480
00:28:32.077 --> 00:28:34.989
So what. they tried to take her out
while the deputy went back to the scene?

481
00:28:35.013 --> 00:28:36.811
Yeah. he went to
fix it up. Found me.

482
00:28:37.082 --> 00:28:38.380
(CELL PHONE RINGS)

483
00:28:39.084 --> 00:28:40.985
Hey. Cass. tell me
you got something

484
00:28:41.220 --> 00:28:43.780
- that doesn't involve chicks in prison.
- (CHUCKLES)

485
00:28:44.256 --> 00:28:46.056
Bet you never thought
you'd say that out loud.

486
00:28:46.425 --> 00:28:47.859
CASTIEL: <i>It's a Nachzehrer.</i>

487
00:28:48.594 --> 00:28:51.860
- Come again?
<i>- A ghoul and vampire-like creature.</i>

488
00:28:52.397 --> 00:28:54.263
A Ghoul-pire! Right?

489
00:28:55.701 --> 00:28:57.381
<i>Some breeds feed on
the flesh of the dead.</i>

490
00:28:57.536 --> 00:28:59.496
<i>Others feed on the blood
and hearts of the living.</i>

491
00:28:59.738 --> 00:29:03.402
<i>They run in small packs. but they
usually keep an extremely low profile.</i>

492
00:29:03.575 --> 00:29:04.775
Great. So. how do we kill 'em?

493
00:29:04.810 --> 00:29:06.250
CASTIEL: <i>Well.
they're already dead.</i>

494
00:29:06.378 --> 00:29:09.378
<i>So in a manner of speaking. they just
need to be reminded that they're dead.</i>

495
00:29:09.648 --> 00:29:11.981
<i>- You need a Charon's obol.</i>
- Of course.

496
00:29:12.718 --> 00:29:15.017
SAM: <i>Yeah. in ancient
Greece. when a person died.</i>

497
00:29:15.187 --> 00:29:17.986
some people believed you had to
put an obol. or a coin in their mouth.

498
00:29:18.156 --> 00:29:21.820
so they could use it as currency to be
taken across the river to the underworld.

499
00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:24.400
CASTIEL: <i>Right. you place a
coin in a Nachzehrer's mouth.</i>

500
00:29:24.496 --> 00:29:26.556
<i>then sever their head.
and that will kill them.</i>

501
00:29:26.732 --> 00:29:28.543
<i>And according to the lore.
if you kill the pack's Alpha.</i>

502
00:29:28.567 --> 00:29:31.036
<i>everyone they've turned will
revert back to human form.</i>

503
00:29:31.203 --> 00:29:33.229
Awesome. All right.
where do we find an obol?

504
00:29:33.639 --> 00:29:35.450
CASTIEL: <i>Well. according
to the Men of Letters' records.</i>

505
00:29:35.474 --> 00:29:37.067
<i>you're gonna need a copper coin.</i>

506
00:29:37.576 --> 00:29:40.011
<i>They used to use pennies.
so. you'll need one of those.</i>

507
00:29:40.746 --> 00:29:42.908
Yeah. but one minted pre-1982.

508
00:29:43.448 --> 00:29:46.941
So before 1982.
pennies were 95% copper.

509
00:29:47.119 --> 00:29:48.839
Since then. they're
only copper-plated zinc.

510
00:29:48.920 --> 00:29:50.965
- Wow. Your nerdiness knows no bounds.
- (SAM SCOFFS)

511
00:29:50.989 --> 00:29:53.458
- You're welcome.
- DEAN: <i>All right. well. thanks. Cass.</i>

512
00:29:54.126 --> 00:29:55.754
Good work. Way to
come off the bench.

513
00:29:55.994 --> 00:29:56.994
CASTIEL: <i>What bench?</i>

514
00:29:57.262 --> 00:29:59.390
Just get back to
getting better. okay?

515
00:30:01.800 --> 00:30:02.800
Got nothing.

516
00:30:03.468 --> 00:30:05.937
Well. yeah. I mean. who carries
pennies these days. anyway?

517
00:30:13.011 --> 00:30:14.445
- I'll be right back.
- DEAN: Yeah.

518
00:30:17.349 --> 00:30:18.715
Mrs. Markham?

519
00:30:19.785 --> 00:30:21.413
- Mrs. Markham. It's okay.
- (GASPING)

520
00:30:21.586 --> 00:30:22.781
I'm Dean Winchester.

521
00:30:22.954 --> 00:30:24.479
- My brother Sam and...
- Where am I?

522
00:30:26.725 --> 00:30:29.718
You were attacked by the same
people that killed your husband.

523
00:30:31.430 --> 00:30:32.430
My husband.

524
00:30:32.898 --> 00:30:35.009
DEAN: <i>Now do you know something
about what happened to him?</i>

525
00:30:35.033 --> 00:30:36.713
<i>Maybe that's why these
people attacked you?</i>

526
00:30:39.504 --> 00:30:40.504
Okay.

527
00:30:41.139 --> 00:30:42.984
Well. we're gonna take you
someplace safe. all right?

528
00:30:43.008 --> 00:30:44.888
And then we're gonna
kill these sons of bitches.

529
00:30:47.045 --> 00:30:48.775
(MUFFLED GROWLING)

530
00:30:51.450 --> 00:30:52.760
- (DONNELLY GROWLING LOUDLY)
- (GASPS)

531
00:30:52.784 --> 00:30:55.219
Whoa. whoa. whoa. I could.
uh... I could explain that.

532
00:30:55.754 --> 00:30:57.265
- Well. maybe not.
- (BREATHING HEAVILY)

533
00:30:57.289 --> 00:30:59.383
<i>Um. it's like the thing
that attacked you. okay?</i>

534
00:30:59.558 --> 00:31:00.924
(STUTTERS) It's a Ghoul-pire.

535
00:31:01.493 --> 00:31:03.004
The point is. it can't
hurt you anymore.

536
00:31:03.028 --> 00:31:05.468
- At least. I don't think it can. It's...
- (MUFFLED GROWLING)

537
00:31:05.497 --> 00:31:07.227
You know what?
Let's just get rid of it.

538
00:31:08.233 --> 00:31:09.565
(SHUDDERS)

539
00:31:10.969 --> 00:31:12.096
Here we go.

540
00:31:24.616 --> 00:31:27.085
Okay. all right.
See? There we go.

541
00:31:28.320 --> 00:31:29.913
- You okay?
- Your family.

542
00:31:31.990 --> 00:31:33.618
You do anything
for them. don't you?

543
00:31:36.361 --> 00:31:37.361
DEAN: <i>Absolutely.</i>

544
00:31:37.796 --> 00:31:40.163
Yeah. but not if it costs
too much. (CHUCKLES)

545
00:31:40.732 --> 00:31:41.756
No.

546
00:31:42.467 --> 00:31:45.198
You do everything for them.
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

547
00:31:46.304 --> 00:31:48.205
Everything else is meaningless.

548
00:31:49.975 --> 00:31:51.273
But I did it wrong.

549
00:31:52.878 --> 00:31:54.506
Now I've ruined everything.

550
00:31:57.015 --> 00:31:58.278
This isn't your fault.

551
00:31:59.317 --> 00:32:00.808
I put my family at risk.

552
00:32:02.454 --> 00:32:04.184
They were right to attack me.

553
00:32:07.659 --> 00:32:09.525
But I know how to make it right.

554
00:32:13.799 --> 00:32:15.131
(BOTH GRUNTING)

555
00:32:15.667 --> 00:32:18.102
Where is it? What did you
do with the maker's body?

556
00:32:19.438 --> 00:32:21.304
You're gonna tell
me or I will end you!

557
00:32:21.640 --> 00:32:22.938
(BOTH GRUNTING)

558
00:32:48.533 --> 00:32:49.933
(TIRES SCREECHING)

559
00:32:50.802 --> 00:32:52.100
- (GUN FIRES)
- (GRUNTS)

560
00:32:58.276 --> 00:32:59.335
(GRUNTS)

561
00:33:01.413 --> 00:33:02.540
(GRUNTS)

562
00:33:03.448 --> 00:33:05.474
See? That wasn't so hard.

563
00:33:06.151 --> 00:33:07.915
Now. I know what to do with you.

564
00:33:09.321 --> 00:33:10.880
(LILY SINGING)

565
00:33:12.224 --> 00:33:13.624
<i>I can make this right</i>

566
00:33:14.793 --> 00:33:16.728
<i>I can make this right</i>

567
00:33:17.762 --> 00:33:18.762
<i>I can make this right</i>

568
00:33:18.964 --> 00:33:20.262
(DONNELLY GASPING)

569
00:33:21.633 --> 00:33:22.828
LILY: <i>You're okay!</i>

570
00:33:23.435 --> 00:33:26.599
See? I fixed it. You're okay.

571
00:33:41.419 --> 00:33:42.648
DONNELLY: <i>I know you're awake.</i>

572
00:33:43.255 --> 00:33:44.985
I know you're a hunter.

573
00:33:49.461 --> 00:33:50.895
(SIGHS)

574
00:33:51.396 --> 00:33:53.331
And I know you're a Nachzehrer.

575
00:33:53.698 --> 00:33:54.825
(DONNELLY LAUGHS)

576
00:33:55.901 --> 00:33:58.735
The maker. right?
The pack Alpha?

577
00:33:59.170 --> 00:34:01.537
Well. maybe you're
not as dumb as you look.

578
00:34:02.340 --> 00:34:04.605
Thought you and yours
like to keep a low profile.

579
00:34:05.410 --> 00:34:08.471
Sadly. rookies like Lily
here aren't up to snuff

580
00:34:08.647 --> 00:34:11.173
when it comes to
keeping their feeding quiet.

581
00:34:11.783 --> 00:34:12.978
So. you killed your husband?

582
00:34:13.351 --> 00:34:14.351
He wouldn't join us.

583
00:34:15.787 --> 00:34:17.483
People who don't join are food.

584
00:34:21.760 --> 00:34:25.458
<i>But. I... I messed up. and
I... I didn't bury him right.</i>

585
00:34:25.730 --> 00:34:27.130
DONNELLY: <i>It's my fault. really.</i>

586
00:34:27.632 --> 00:34:29.362
You weren't properly trained.

587
00:34:30.268 --> 00:34:33.329
DONNELLY: (CHUCKLES) <i>But
everyone deserves a mulligan. don't they?</i>

588
00:34:34.839 --> 00:34:36.933
That's all my people
were trying to do. Lily.

589
00:34:37.108 --> 00:34:38.974
They weren't going to kill you.

590
00:34:39.277 --> 00:34:40.575
Hell. I need you.

591
00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:44.482
I need all the help I can get.

592
00:34:44.783 --> 00:34:46.012
How many have you turned?

593
00:34:46.351 --> 00:34:49.014
In the first 100 years? Three.

594
00:34:49.988 --> 00:34:52.787
In the last month? Sixteen.

595
00:34:53.158 --> 00:34:54.958
What. are you trying
to field a baseball team?

596
00:34:54.993 --> 00:34:59.761
It's like I said. I need help.
every strong hand I can find.

597
00:35:02.200 --> 00:35:07.901
And I need an army
to fight The Darkness.

598
00:35:10.709 --> 00:35:13.235
Oh. it's comin'. for all of us.

599
00:35:14.379 --> 00:35:17.816
There's nothing hunters or
any human can do about it.

600
00:35:19.351 --> 00:35:20.751
Do you know how to stop it?

601
00:35:21.653 --> 00:35:23.622
I don't think
anything can stop it.

602
00:35:25.724 --> 00:35:28.319
<i>I'm just tryin' to
buy some time.</i>

603
00:35:28.493 --> 00:35:32.294
so I'm turning as many strong
men and women as I can.

604
00:35:33.598 --> 00:35:37.035
Your brother will make a fine
addition to the rank and file.

605
00:35:39.004 --> 00:35:43.271
While you slept. I sent him a
text message from your phone.

606
00:35:46.411 --> 00:35:48.539
<i>Oh. he's heading
into a trap right now.</i>

607
00:35:49.381 --> 00:35:51.680
You'd make a good soldier. too.

608
00:35:53.585 --> 00:35:56.646
But you cut off my head.
and I can't stand for that.

609
00:35:57.922 --> 00:35:58.922
<i>Don't worry.</i>

610
00:36:00.225 --> 00:36:03.593
I'm an "every part of
the buffalo" kind of guy.

611
00:36:04.362 --> 00:36:06.024
Your death won't go to waste.

612
00:36:08.400 --> 00:36:10.392
You'll be your
brother's first meal.

613
00:36:11.536 --> 00:36:12.799
(DONNELLY LAUGHS)

614
00:36:14.639 --> 00:36:16.073
- (BOTH GRUNTING)
- (LILY GASPS)

615
00:36:16.908 --> 00:36:18.001
(TIRES SCREECHING)

616
00:36:19.678 --> 00:36:20.976
(CRASHING)

617
00:36:30.655 --> 00:36:32.055
(DEAN GRUNTING)

618
00:37:14.032 --> 00:37:15.193
(DONNELLY GROWLING)

619
00:37:15.567 --> 00:37:17.058
(BOTH GRUNTING)

620
00:37:22.040 --> 00:37:23.040
(THUDDING)

621
00:37:25.643 --> 00:37:27.134
(GLASS SHATTERING)

622
00:37:28.747 --> 00:37:30.443
(BOTH GRUNTING)

623
00:37:32.450 --> 00:37:33.679
(LILY GRUNTING)

624
00:37:34.352 --> 00:37:35.684
(ALL GRUNTING)

625
00:37:59.277 --> 00:38:00.336
(SCREAMS)

626
00:38:00.812 --> 00:38:01.939
(GROANS)

627
00:38:08.486 --> 00:38:09.852
(DONNELLY GROWLING)

628
00:38:10.989 --> 00:38:12.480
(DONNELLY GRUNTING)

629
00:38:16.394 --> 00:38:17.885
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

630
00:38:20.465 --> 00:38:21.465
(SIGHING)

631
00:38:29.340 --> 00:38:30.899
Oh. baby. I'm so sorry.

632
00:38:31.176 --> 00:38:32.176
(GROANING)

633
00:38:41.452 --> 00:38:42.613
Oh. my God. What have I...

634
00:38:46.291 --> 00:38:47.291
My kids.

635
00:38:48.326 --> 00:38:50.454
My kids. They turned my
kids. They're with the others.

636
00:38:50.895 --> 00:38:51.919
Please.

637
00:38:52.463 --> 00:38:53.522
Sam.

638
00:38:55.400 --> 00:38:56.400
Yeah. yeah.

639
00:39:01.272 --> 00:39:02.272
(SIGHS)

640
00:39:02.807 --> 00:39:03.866
(LILY SIGHS)

641
00:39:09.013 --> 00:39:10.379
(ENGINE SPUTTERING)

642
00:39:11.316 --> 00:39:12.375
(GRUNTS)

643
00:39:14.219 --> 00:39:16.654
- (ENGINE SPUTTERING)
- Come on. Come on. Come on.

644
00:39:16.988 --> 00:39:18.183
(ENGINE DIES)

645
00:39:19.991 --> 00:39:21.323
(ENGINE SPUTTERING)

646
00:39:21.726 --> 00:39:24.025
- Come on. baby. Yeah! There we go.
- (ENGINE STARTING)

647
00:39:24.863 --> 00:39:25.990
(SIGHS DEEPLY)

648
00:39:28.666 --> 00:39:29.666
Ah.

649
00:39:36.074 --> 00:39:37.235
Hang on.

650
00:39:41.346 --> 00:39:42.871
(TIRES SQUEALING)

651
00:40:04.636 --> 00:40:05.865
(GASPS)

652
00:40:08.840 --> 00:40:09.840
(LAUGHS)

653
00:40:12.644 --> 00:40:13.737
BOY: Mom!

654
00:40:14.112 --> 00:40:15.171
(LILY LAUGHS)

655
00:40:15.546 --> 00:40:18.072
- GIRL: You okay?
- Probably nothing. right?

656
00:40:19.117 --> 00:40:20.710
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

657
00:40:21.152 --> 00:40:23.212
- DEAN: Everybody all right back there?
- Uh. yeah.

658
00:40:23.388 --> 00:40:24.856
They all changed back.

659
00:40:25.356 --> 00:40:26.380
(SIGHS)

660
00:40:26.691 --> 00:40:28.717
So. it was Deputy Dumbass. huh?

661
00:40:28.993 --> 00:40:32.122
(GRUNTS) Yeah. Deputy Dumbass.
You know. he was trying to build an army.

662
00:40:32.397 --> 00:40:34.923
Yeah. I know. To
fight The Darkness.

663
00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.901
Dean. even the
monsters are scared.

664
00:40:38.102 --> 00:40:39.102
Well. let 'em be.

665
00:40:40.438 --> 00:40:43.306
You and I. we're gonna
end this thing now.

666
00:40:44.776 --> 00:40:47.871
You. you mind starting
tomorrow? (CHUCKLES)

667
00:40:49.380 --> 00:40:52.145
- Deal.
- Deal. (CHUCKLES)

668
00:40:52.583 --> 00:40:53.744
We'll get Cass to fix you up.

669
00:40:54.552 --> 00:40:56.180
Only if he fixes you up. too.

670
00:40:57.522 --> 00:40:58.854
Okay. Mom.

671
00:40:59.357 --> 00:41:00.381
Let's go home.

672
00:41:01.025 --> 00:41:03.824
You know what? We are home.

673
00:41:05.964 --> 00:41:07.557
(ENGINE SPUTTERING)

674
00:41:09.667 --> 00:41:11.101
Come on. Come on.

675
00:41:12.236 --> 00:41:13.864
- (ENGINE STARTS)
- Ah.

676
00:41:14.172 --> 00:41:15.172
There's my girl.

677
00:41:18.576 --> 00:41:20.135
<i>(NIGHT MOVES</i> PLAYING)

678
00:42:23.775 --> 00:42:24.775
English-SDH

